5	 *
6	 * <p>Used for the owner's {@code checkDigit}, computed over the digits of its
7	 * {@code customerCode}. Non-digit characters are ignored, so the separators in a code such as
8	 * {@code 'SYD-SMI-0007'} do not contribute; the rightmost digit is doubled first per the
9	 * standard Luhn algorithm.
